      "label": "Mullite",
      "category_type": "ACTOR_TERM",
      "definition_short": "An aluminum silicate ceramic (Al₆Si₂O₁₃) created when kaolinitic clay is fired above 1,300°C. Medieval Hessian crucible makers unwittingly synthesized mullite, achieving superior thermal and chemical resistance. Formally identified in 20th century; medieval mastery was empirical.",
